 "title": "Adding and subtracting polynomials",
 "audience": "learner",
 "keyIdea": "Add or subtract polynomials by combining like terms; when subtracting, change the sign of every term in the second polynomial.",
 "explain": {
  "kid": [
   "Like terms have the same letter and the same power, like 3x² and 5x². You can add them: 8x².",
   "x² and x are not like terms. Keep them apart, like apples and oranges."
  ],
  "adult": [
   "To add, group like terms: (3x² + 2x − 1) + (x² − 5x + 4) = 4x² − 3x + 3.",
   "To subtract, the minus sign hits every term in the second bracket. So (5x² + x − 4) − (2x² − 3x + 1) = 5x² + x − 4 − 2x² + 3x − 1 = 3x² + 4x − 5."
  ]
 },
